  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "A unitary divisor of $n$ is $d\\mid n$ such that $(d,n/d)=1$. A number $n\\geq 1$ is a unitary perfect number if it is the sum of its unitary divisors (aside from $n$ itself).\nAre there only finite many unitary perfect numbers?",
